  "question": "If $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are two unit vectors such that $|\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}| = \\sqrt{3}$, then the angle between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ is:",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "$|\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}|^2 = |\\vec{a}|^2 + |\\vec{b}|^2 - 2\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}$<br /><br />$= 1 + 1 - 2\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = 2 - 2\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />Given $|\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}| = \\sqrt{3}$<br /><br />$\\implies (\\sqrt{3})^2 = 2 - 2\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />$3 = 2 - 2\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />$\\implies 2\\cos\\theta = 2 - 3 = -1$<br /><br />$\\implies \\cos\\theta = -\\frac{1}{2}$<br /><br />$\\implies \\theta = 120^\\circ$<br /><br />Correct option: D.",
